WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.120
It had been the same nightmare for weeks now,
but always fading into echoes as he awoke.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.200
Not tonight, though.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:13.130
Tonight, he was able to see more, to hold
on to the details of his dark, twisted dream…

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.160
and the warning it contained.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:20.280
Doctor Stephen Strange had once been an accomplished
surgeon, yet fate had destined him to become

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.970
the Sorcerer Supreme of Earth after a car
accident claimed the use of his hands.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:30.910
Now, Strange was a protector of his world
and countless others in the vast expanse of

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:36.050
the multiverse, a master of the mystic arts
wielding his skills in sorcerer and arcane

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.789
artifacts to defend against malevolent otherworldly
threats.

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:43.780
But even he had never seen anything like this
nightmare before.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.949
On the night when the details of the dream
felt easier to keep a hold on, a sleeping

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:50.739
Stephen was shown all manner of horrors.

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:55.950
The world he had devoted himself to protecting
was crumbling, burning, all around was death

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:01.010
and suffering, the air shrill with the screams
of tortured innocent souls.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.930
To make matters worse, within the dream, Strange
could feel the same suffering reaching out,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:11.250
crossing the boundaries between realities;
it wasn’t just his world he saw dying, it

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.720
was all of them, every corner of the multiverse
falling.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.250
It turned his stomach.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:22.119
It all felt so real, not just an anxious,
unconscious fantasy of something he feared

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:23.620
might happen.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.450
This was a warning, of something that would
come to pass.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:33.140
The dread felt by the Sorcerer Supreme only
got worse as he witnessed a familiar figure,

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:38.340
injured and broken, crawling free of the rubble
of a destroyed city, the flickering light

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.890
of endless fires doing little to mask the
man’s wounds.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:46.560
Instantly, Doctor Strange recognized the wounded
figure from the distinctive flared cloak he

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.799
wore to his goatee and dark hair greying at
the temples – it was him, or rather, another

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:56.899
version of him from a different reality within
the multiverse.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:59.820
“H-help,” the other Strange said weakly.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.280
Instantly, Stephen knelt to help his interdimensional
doppelganger up.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.570
“What happened here?” he asked, concerned
at the vision of destruction all around.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:11.960
“I couldn’t stop it,” the ‘Messenger
Strange’ replied in labored breaths; he

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.690
was wounded, fatally, barely holding on.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:19.100
“Slow down, breathe,” Doctor Strange calmly
instructed his other self, still retaining

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.340
a bedside manner from his days as a surgeon.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.660
“This vision, I take it you’re trying
to warn me of something?”

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.890
“Yes,” the dying sorcerer replied.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.620
“I cast a spell that should reach you in
your sleep, although sending a message across

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.700
the multiverse is -” he paused to wince
in pain, feeling his already fading strength

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.940
dwindling further.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.690
“It takes a lot more than I have left.”

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.090
“It’s alright,” Strange assured him.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.000
“I can hear you; I’m listening.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.050
I only wish I could do more for you.”

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.550
“It’s alright,” his variant forced a
weak smile.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.330
“By the time this message reaches you, I’ll
already have been dead.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.950
But you needed to be warned…”

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.550
“What happened here?”

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:55.550
Strange urged.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.330
“It’s not what has happened.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.800
It’s what’s coming.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.319
It had to be us… of course, it did,” the
other’s breaths started slowing.

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:05.840
“I tried everything; I really did.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:06.840
But he…

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.239
I’ve never felt power like it.”

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:10.970
“Just tell me who!”

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:14.840
Stephen shouted, aware his other self was
fading fast, desperate to hear the full warning

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.610
before the dream ended.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:20.450
Already Doctor Strange’s mind was racing
with potential candidates who could have been

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.500
responsible.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.560
He knew of a plethora of deities and destructive
creatures capable of launching attacks on

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.370
his home universe, and many who had time and
time again.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:35.250
There were the likes of Nightmare and Shuma-Gorath,
and of course, his arch-nemesis Dormammu,

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.180
an entity who had long desired total control
over the plane of existence Stephen’s Earth

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.180
inhabited.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.310
But not one of them had the power to subjugate
the entire multiverse in one fell swoop.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:50.010
“Please…” Messenger Strange rasped,
leaning up to Stephen’s ear.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.069
“Don’t make the same mistake I did.

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:53.069
Beware…

00:03:53.069 --> 00:03:54.260
beware the Scarlet King.”

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:59.191
He collapsed, his breathing stopped as Doctor
Strange looked at the horrific sight of a

00:03:59.191 --> 00:04:04.390
man almost identical to him dying, having
failed to prevent the chaos that was now consuming

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.480
everything.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:10.450
The Sorcerer Supreme had an encyclopedic knowledge
of the mystic arts, and all kinds of occult

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.560
beings, but had never heard of the Scarlet
King.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:19.570
As he woke up in a cold sweat, still feeling
the same dread he had felt in the dream, Doctor

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.690
Strange could remember the warning from his
other multiversal self.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.210
It had to be him.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.830
He had to stop the Scarlet King.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.320
“The Scarlet who?”

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.850
repeated Wong, Stephen’s trusted friend
and confident, an expert in both mystic and

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.730
martial arts, as well as an accomplished scholar.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.350
“Scarlet King, the other me was adamant
that this thing had to be stopped by another

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:42.060
version of me,” Doctor Strange explained.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.510
Having woken up flustered and with growing
concern over his vision, Stephen had spent

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.580
the whole morning in the library.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:52.810
The Sanctum Sanctorum had long been Strange’s
home and base of operations since he had inherited

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.850
the title of Sorcerer Supreme from the Ancient
One.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.570
Additionally, the magical building in the
heart of New York’s Greenwich Village also

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.470
possessed a sprawling library filled with
tomes that contained what was thought to be

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.520
the sum total of all occult knowledge.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:11.600
His books were filled with useful information
on spells, other planes of existence, even

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.520
detailing accounts of threats Stephen had
already faced, like Dormammu.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.690
And yet, there was no mention of any ‘Scarlet
King.’

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:22.539
“I don’t understand it, my other self,
he mentioned it specifically by name, but

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:26.860
I can’t find a single reference to it in
any texts,” Strange sighed in frustration.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:31.100
“The Book of Cagliostro, nothing, no mention
of a Scarlet King.”

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.860
“Strange,” Wong mused.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.860
“What?”

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.860
Stephen replied.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.210
“No, I mean it’s unusual you found nothing,”
his friend answered, trying to hide a smile

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.259
at catching Stephen in a joke.

00:05:40.259 --> 00:05:42.610
“Perhaps the Book of Vishanti holds more
answers?

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:46.250
It contains all of the knowledge the great
sorcerer Agamotto collected on the mystic-”

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.810
“Nope, I already tried that,” Doctor Strange
interrupted.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.940
“I consulted our copy of the Darkhold too
while I was at it.”

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.430
“You did what?”

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:57.500
Wong exclaimed, ever concerned by Stephen’s
arrogant and reckless behavior.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.250
The Darkhold was a dangerous tome, a book
of spells used only for pure evil, written

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.760
by an elder god named Chthon.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.750
Even though the original, true Darkhold was
out of reach, the knowledge contained within

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:12.560
the copy Stephen possessed was still perilous
to be exposed to.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:17.130
“Oh, relax,” Strange replied in a rather
blasé manner, still absent-mindedly flicking

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:20.000
through the pages of another book, the Codex
Imperium.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.740
“Damn it, I need to know what it is I’m
up against!” he yelled in frustration.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.870
“Wong, you didn’t see what I saw in that
dream.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:29.380
It was chaos, destruction unlike anything
I’ve ever felt before…”

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:32.440
“I understand, Stephen,” his fellow sorcerer
answered.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:36.330
“And as Sorcerer Supreme, you hold a duty
to protect this reality from those that would

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.710
seek to threaten its safety.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.930
But this is dangerous.

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:45.130
A being we know nothing about is rare, perhaps
consider if there is a reason why we know

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.050
nothing of this Scarlet King.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.750
There is some knowledge that it is not meant
to be uncovered.”

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.470
“Knowledge is power, old friend,” Doctor
Strange retorted.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.900
“And if I’m going to do my duty to protect
our reality, I need to know anything that

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:56.900
will give me an edge.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.370
I’ll be in my study.”

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:02.340
With that, the Sorcerer Supreme strode off
to a private corner of the Sanctum.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:07.680
He spent the next few restless hours using
his mastery of the occult to peer at the future.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:11.770
Understanding the mystical mechanics of time
in the way he did meant Stephen was aware

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:17.100
that there was no singular future, but rather
millions upon millions of possible outcomes,

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:21.740
a web of potential courses that fate could
take, and any decision made could create a

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.210
new strand in this already tangled mess.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.960
Still, there was no outcome where any Scarlet
King existed.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:33.129
However, it was then that Doctor Strange realized
what he had been missing, a detail so small

00:07:33.129 --> 00:07:37.910
that it had gone unnoticed but so crucial
that it changed his entire approach.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:43.599
He had been thinking of the situation entirely
wrong, in an insular fashion that focused

00:07:43.599 --> 00:07:46.770
solely on his own reality, his universe.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:52.810
But the warning had come from across the multiverse,
from another Strange in another world.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:57.000
What’s more was the feeling, the sense he’d
felt during the nightmare.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.910
Although he knew nothing of his enemy, Strange
could tell that the destruction the Scarlet

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:05.430
King was capable of had the reach to threaten
all corners of the multiverse.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:09.379
This wasn’t just a threat to his world,
but all worlds.

00:08:09.379 --> 00:08:13.650
Strange’s search for answers about the Scarlet
King had proved fruitless thus far.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:18.050
Yet, remembering this was a threat coming
from across the vastness of the infinite multiverse

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:24.410
oddly seemed to provide some comfort; because
there was one entity he did know of, who might

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.310
be able to help.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.080
Hands aglow with magic, Doctor Strange performed
the correct ritual he knew would allow him

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.539
to commune with the Living Tribunal.

00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:37.310
Sure enough, the room around him faded away,
and he was presented with the highest authority

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.719
in the multiverse.

00:08:38.719 --> 00:08:43.810
The towering, vastly powerful entity was humanoid
in shape, save for a head floating separate

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:50.250
from its shoulders, with three faces; one
fully hooded, one half, and the other uncovered.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.519
The Sorcerer Supreme had conversed on a few
occasions with the entity, enough to know

00:08:54.519 --> 00:08:59.550
it was responsible for safeguarding the multiverse,
to prevent universes from amassing too much

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:04.769
power in case they threatened others, maintaining
balance, which made the fact it had done nothing

00:09:04.769 --> 00:09:08.470
to prevent the imminent danger of the Scarlet
King all the more concerning.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:11.230
“Speak, Strange,” the Tribunal’s booming
voice commanded, speaking from its front,

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.230
unhooded face.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:13.230
“Living Tribunal.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.330
I have come seeking answers,” Doctor Strange
replied.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:20.220
“There is a being, an entity that poses
a threat to my world and all others in the

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.220
multiverse.”

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:27.130
“I am not aware of such a threat,” the
multiversal arbiter replied.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.200
“Please!”

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.200
Strange urged.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.460
“It’s out there, and I need to be the
one to stop it.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:36.580
There’s no information on it in my universe,
so I ask you, please tell me where I can find

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.580
someone…

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.920
anyone who knows about the Scarlet King…”

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:43.500
There was silence for a moment as the different
faces of the Living Tribunal conferred.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.700
All three had to agree on whether or not it
could interfere.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:53.240
“The answers you seek lie beyond your universe,”
the Tribunal finally answered.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.580
“We are… in agreement.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.510
I will send you there.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:01.430
But exercise caution, Stephen Strange…”

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:05.470
In a flash, Doctor Strange had appeared somewhere
new.

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:08.820
The room was dark, filthy, nothing short of
bleak.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:13.200
But still, it was a far cry from the devastation
he had seen in his vision.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.440
The walls were covered in scribbled writing,
that had seemingly been scrawled over every

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.490
surface by someone in a state of madness.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:25.649
There was one that caught Doctor Strange’s
attention: a figure, adorned in red armor,

00:10:25.649 --> 00:10:28.130
large antler-like horns protruding from his
head.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.912
It didn’t take someone with as much knowledge
of the Sorcerer Supreme to know that this

00:10:31.912 --> 00:10:34.589
was a drawing of the illusive Scarlet King
himself.

00:10:34.589 --> 00:10:35.589
“Who’s there?”

00:10:35.589 --> 00:10:37.750
A voice rasped.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:42.380
Stephen turned to see an old man, withered
and alone, laying on a grimy hospital bed

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:43.850
in a corner of the room.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:49.360
“Sorry, I didn’t see you,” he said calmly,
cautiously approaching, only lowering his

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:52.280
guard when he heard the elderly man give a
hoarse throat.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.600
“You’re very sick,” Strange remarked.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.279
“Dying, I should think,” the man replied.

00:10:57.279 --> 00:10:59.060
“Are you Foundation?”

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.220
“Foundation?”

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.860
the sorcerer echoed in confusion.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:06.700
“Yes, yes, don’t be surprised, I know
all about them,” the anonymous man said

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:07.700
weakly.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.270
“I haven’t forgotten when I used to work
there.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:15.740
Or how they feel about what I know… they’d
stop at nothing to silence me.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:17.510
God knows they’ve tried over the years.”

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:22.149
“Listen, I was sent here because I need
answers,” Doctor Strange interrupted, aware

00:11:22.149 --> 00:11:24.910
of the impending threat he felt the need to
avert.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.910
“So, Mister-”
“Doctor!”

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.000
the old man corrected.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.089
“Doctor Robert Montauk.”

00:11:31.089 --> 00:11:33.050
“Doctor Montauk,” Stephen echoed.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:36.030
“What can you tell me about the Scarlet
King?”

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:41.470
Montauk started chuckling, a dry, wheezing
sound, almost like he was taunting the sorcerer.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:46.310
His laughter lasted far longer than that of
a sane man; paired with the drawings and markings

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:50.640
on the walls, Stephen was certain something
inside Robert Montauk was broken.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.240
“Oh, I could tell you so much about the
Scarlet King, I was one of his Children once…

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:02.430
so long ago now,” he sighed, a loud, hacking
cough brought on by his laugher, forcing its

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:04.529
way out of Montauk’s throat.

00:12:04.529 --> 00:12:08.149
“But that’s his strength, you see.

00:12:08.149 --> 00:12:10.650
Being known, being understood.”

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:13.150
“Look, this being is threatening my world.

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.420
I need to know how I’m supposed to stop
him?”

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.800
Strange asked.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.430
“Stop him?”

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.220
Doctor Montauk chuckled at him.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.829
“What makes you think you can?”

00:12:22.829 --> 00:12:25.839
“I was told I have to,” the Sorcerer Supreme
admitted.

00:12:25.839 --> 00:12:27.089
“It has to be me.

00:12:27.089 --> 00:12:30.850
And if you won’t tell me what I need to
know, then I’m very sorry.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.430
Normally I’d never do this, but in the grand
calculus of the multiverse, there is nothing

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.270
I won’t sacrifice to protect it.”

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:40.860
With a wave of his hands, Doctor Strange conjured
his third eye, which snapped open in the centre

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.050
of his forehead.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:46.480
It functioned as an organic manifestation
of his amulet, the powerful mystical artifact

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.649
known as the Eye of Agamotto.

00:12:48.649 --> 00:12:53.089
And through it, Stephen peered into Doctor
Montauk’s fractured mind, seeking out the

00:12:53.089 --> 00:12:56.060
information he was withholding about the Scarlet
King.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.220
“No, no, you can’t!”

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:02.779
Montauk shouted, his frail, withered hands
gripping his temples as he felt the sorcerer

00:13:02.779 --> 00:13:04.279
invading his memories.

00:13:04.279 --> 00:13:05.960
“I’m sorry,” Strange repeated.

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:09.400
“But knowledge is power, and I need to know
how to stop the Scarlet King.”

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.630
“You think knowledge is power?”

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:12.680
the old man rasped.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.190
“It’s more than that to him.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:16.740
It’s a weapon… his weapon.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.370
The more we know him…”

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:19.490
It was too late.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.110
Doctor Strange had found what he was looking
for.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:27.260
Years earlier, Doctor Robert Montauk had been
working at the SCP Foundation and had uncovered

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:33.870
the true nature of SCP-001, Tufto’s Proposal,
otherwise known as the Scarlet King.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:38.949
The King was an elder god, a force of pure
chaos and the manifestation of a hatred for

00:13:38.949 --> 00:13:39.949
modernity.

00:13:39.949 --> 00:13:41.899
But it was far worse than that…

00:13:41.899 --> 00:13:47.620
A huge, crimson crack split through the concrete
wall, a doorway to the Scarlet King’s domain.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:52.430
Pulling himself out of Robert Montauk’s
mind the second he realized his mistake, Doctor

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.380
Strange was still reeling as the portal opened.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.690
How could he have been so stupid?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.580
His nightmare hadn’t been a warning to prevent
what was coming, it was either a warning to

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.030
stay away… or a trap.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:06.230
Snapping back to awareness, Stephen found
he was no longer in the filthy room where

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:08.570
the dying Doctor Montauk lay.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:13.660
Instead, he was in a vast multiversal void,
a space between universes.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:18.579
And there, among the huge expanse of nothingness,
stood the Scarlet King.

00:14:18.579 --> 00:14:24.089
He towered above Doctor Strange, his physical
form adorned in armor the shade of blood.

00:14:24.089 --> 00:14:29.040
Atop his head was a crown-like ornament, the
large antlers jutting out above.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:33.959
His hands were gnarled claws, clenched into
massive fists, and his many eyes were looking

00:14:33.959 --> 00:14:35.399
at Stephen.

00:14:35.399 --> 00:14:39.649
Having seen inside Montauk’s mind, Doctor
Strange had realized all too late that the

00:14:39.649 --> 00:14:42.470
Scarlet King was more than just an ancient
evil being.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:43.470
He was a living idea, given form by every
attempt to study, quantify and define exactly

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:44.470
what the King was.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:45.470
He was the very notion of nihilism, shaped
by a hatred of the modern world and a desire

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:49.079
to return to a more violent age, but if nobody
talked about him, he would gain no further

00:14:49.079 --> 00:14:50.079
power.

00:14:50.079 --> 00:14:54.220
The Scarlet King had only grown in strength
the more the SCP Foundation had tried to learn

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:55.310
about him.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.500
And now, the Sorcerer Supreme himself had
done the same.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:03.370
The King had achieved even greater power thanks
to Strange falling into his trap, enough to

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:06.279
open up a gateway and bring him here.

00:15:06.279 --> 00:15:10.660
“You already know, don’t you, sorcerer?”

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:16.370
the Scarlet King snarled, his voice sounding
like billions upon billions of insects chittering.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:20.860
“Through Montauk, you know.”

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:24.459
Stephen looked in horror at the interdimensional
abomination.

00:15:24.459 --> 00:15:29.319
Even just by observing him, being able to
perceive his physical form, he was unintentionally

00:15:29.319 --> 00:15:30.790
empowering the entity.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:35.569
But living idea or not, Strange had seen the
destruction that the Scarlet King could unfurl

00:15:35.569 --> 00:15:36.820
on the multiverse.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:41.259
“By the Hoary Hosts of Hoggoth,” Doctor
Strange declared, summoning up a spell that

00:15:41.259 --> 00:15:43.740
he hoped would reverse whatever power the
King possessed.

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:47.550
“You will not harm my world, nor any others!”

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:51.310
Unleashing his magic in a blast of light,
the beam struck the Scarlet King.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:56.199
The elder god was harmed, but not undone;
the forces of the mystic arts being almost

00:15:56.199 --> 00:16:00.860
as ancient as the Scarlet King was, and thus,
he could still be hurt.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:04.699
The Scarlet King raised a mighty fist, bringing
it slamming down towards Stephen.

00:16:04.699 --> 00:16:09.990
He was barely able to cast the Shield of Seraphim,
creating a protective circle of mystical energy

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:13.970
that formed a barrier between Strange and
the oncoming attack.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:18.589
As the descending, gigantic fist of the Scarlet
King was deflected, he instantly brought his

00:16:18.589 --> 00:16:21.029
other down in a vicious attack.

00:16:21.029 --> 00:16:26.230
The sheer force of it broke Stephen’s concentration,
causing the Shield to dissipate, barely withstanding

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:30.290
enough of the King’s physical strength to
prevent the Sorcerer from being knocked down.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:35.279
It was like one magically powered ant fighting
against a being impossibly bigger, that could

00:16:35.279 --> 00:16:38.149
stomp Strange out of existence in seconds.

00:16:38.149 --> 00:16:43.399
But even falling to the imperceptible ground
of the void, Doctor Strange didn’t let up,

00:16:43.399 --> 00:16:47.670
refusing to relent and let the Scarlet King
unleash his wrath on the multiverse.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:52.740
His Cloak of Levitation lifted him back to
his feet, and with a wave of both hands, Stephen

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:57.920
burst into multiple astral-projected copies
of himself: the Images of Ikonn.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:03.149
The multiple Doctor Stranges floated independently
through the air, surrounding the Scarlet King.

00:17:03.149 --> 00:17:07.880
Then, as every Stephen gave an outward flick
of his wrist, the Crimson Bands of Cyttorak

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.470
flew from their hands.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:14.040
The bright red belts of energy, virtually
indestructible, bound the powerful, chaotic

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.940
King, lashing around his physical form.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:19.990
But still, Doctor Strange being able to see
and perceive the Scarlet King was granting

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.730
his adversary power.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:26.290
He pulled with all his physical strength,
the Crimson Bands starting to wane, slackening

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:30.090
despite Strange’s efforts to keep all his
duplicates holding on.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:34.760
Gripping the bands in his huge, gnarled hands,
the Scarlet King swung the multiple Stranges

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:39.910
around, forcing them all back into the same,
singular body as they collided.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:44.210
Still holding the one remaining Crimson Band
of Cyttorak, the Scarlet King started to drag

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.720
Stephen towards him.

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:48.830
The King didn’t want him dead, Strange knew
it.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:53.840
He’d be tortured, made and unmade even until
the entity forced him to use his third eye

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.530
again, like he had done to Doctor Montauk.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:18:00.850
If Doctor Strange could fully comprehend the
Scarlet King’s nature, origin, and ideology,

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:04.350
then the King would be able to achieve his
full strength.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.670
That was the trap the Sorcerer Supreme had
been lured into.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:12.150
His own arrogance, his need to be the one
who saved the multiverse, the man holding

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:17.270
the scalpel, was a weakness the Scarlet King
was prepared to exploit in order to achieve

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:20.500
the power he needed to overthrow the multiverse.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:25.360
There was only one thing left that Doctor
Strange could do, one last ditch effort.

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:28.860
It was a long shot, but he hoped it would
be enough.

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:33.510
Releasing his remaining band, Stephen began
casting a spell to send a message to another

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:36.220
of his selves somewhere else in the multiverse.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:39.600
He could hear the Scarlet King looming behind
him, ready to strike.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:44.460
Maybe the King would kill him, but Strange
wouldn’t let that stop him casting the spell.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:48.490
His warning would reach his other self even
after death, in the form of a dream.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:54.020
A warning not to make the same mistake as
this Strange had; to not go searching for

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.120
the Scarlet King.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:19:02.050
Now go and check out “DEADPOOL VS SCP-682”
and “SCP-001 - The Scarlet King” for more

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.080
wild battles and eldritch monsters!

